// error
// #4696: two sibling calls to one bounded generic, standing in ONE template
// body, are one cause and are reported once.
//
// `twiceBound<i64>` is one emitted body and `inner<i64>` is one emitted
// instance, but `vInstJudgeCall` (validateinstchain.bit) judges a call NODE and
// `vInstWalk` visits both. Both diagnostics carried the identical primary span
// and the identical message; only the note's column differed, naming first one
// `inner(v)` and then the other — one root cause the user fixes on one line,
// reported twice.
//
// The descent's dedup could not cover it. `vInstClaim`'s `body` claim is taken
// in `vInstDescend`, and the judgement runs BEFORE the descent and a broken
// bound stops the descent entirely, so the second call node was judged from
// scratch. The judgement now takes a claim of its own, on the same
// (declaration, substituted type arguments) key under a `bound` kind.
//
// THE SECOND CALL IN `main` IS THE OTHER HALF OF THE RULE. `twiceBound(true)`
// is a second ledger entry naming the same template body, and a dedup that
// keyed the pass rather than the entry would swallow it — two different user
// calls are two causes, each fixable on its own line, and both are still
// reported. `_tests_/cases/check_generic_transitive_bound.bit` pins that pair
// for the depth-1 shape.
interface Named {
  label(): string,
}

fn inner<T: Named>(v: T): string {
  return v.label()
}

fn twiceBound<T>(v: T): string {
  return inner(v) + inner(v)
}

fn main() {
  print("${twiceBound(7)}\n")
  print("${twiceBound(true)}\n")
}
